/*
 * Migration: fix metadata for External assets that were created with wrong values
 * by the previous (buggy) parsers.storage.assetRegistry.getAssetLocationsMany
 * implementation. Source of truth is the staging environment (orca-delta-103),
 * which already runs the fixed parser and has the correct multilocation-derived
 * metadata for every External asset.
 *
 * Affected fields (per user request):
 *   - multi_location_ids
 *   - multi_locations_metadata
 *   - multi_locations
 *   - name
 *   - symbol
 *   - decimals
 *   - is_sufficient
 *   - existential_deposit
 *   - xcm_rate_limit
 *
 * Why these specifically:
 *  - multi_locations is the actual XCM multilocation that the buggy parser
 *    was getting wrong (252 of 584 External assets affected). It is the root
 *    cause; everything else here is downstream metadata derived alongside it.
 *  - decimals drives every normalized volume / TVL / spot price calculation
 *    (174 of 584 assets affected) and is the metric-critical field.
 *  - The remaining fields (name, symbol, multi_location_ids,
 *    multi_locations_metadata, is_sufficient, existential_deposit,
 *    xcm_rate_limit) were polluted by the same root cause and are corrected
 *    in the same pass to keep the asset row internally consistent.
 *
 * Idempotency:
 *  - Embedded payload covers ALL External assets in the source-of-truth DB
 *    (584 rows at the time this migration was generated).
 *  - INNER JOIN against the asset table means rows that do not exist on the
 *    target DB are silently skipped (the "if not existing => skip" rule).
 *  - The IS DISTINCT FROM predicate makes re-runs no-ops: if every field
 *    already matches the source-of-truth value, the row is not touched.
 *  - asset_type is intentionally not gated in the WHERE clause: the embedded
 *    set is already restricted to External assets on the source side, and
 *    the id JOIN is the actual filter.
 *
 * Reorg safety:
 *  - Only the asset table is touched. Asset rows are not part of any rolling
 *    cumulative chain and the indexer's batch flow uses a per-batch cache for
 *    asset reads, so the corrected values flow through naturally on the next
 *    batch after deploy.
 *
 * Notes for downstream metric consumers:
 *  - Historical xykpool_volume_historical_data, omnipool_asset_volume_historical_data,
 *    asset_volume_historical_data, asset_spot_price_historical_data and any
 *    rolling *_total_*_norm columns for the 174 decimals-changed assets will
 *    be discontinuous at the deploy block: pre-fix rows keep their old (wrong)
 *    normalization; post-fix rows are computed at the corrected scale and
 *    layered on top of the pre-fix cumulative base. External assets are not a
 *    UI priority, so this is accepted by the project.
 *
 * Embedding format note:
 *  - Each entry of SOURCE_OF_TRUTH below is a JS string holding JSON. We parse
 *    them at module load. Encoding rows as JS string literals (double-JSON
 *    encoded at generation time) avoids template-literal escape ambiguity for
 *    rows that contain backslashes, backticks, or pre-escaped sub-payloads
 *    (e.g. a "network" field whose value is itself a JSON-encoded string).
 */

